  "id": "29-go-err-shadowed",
  "title": "Shadowed err makes validation failure invisible",
  "language": "go",
  "status": "pilot",
  "provenance": {
    "type": "seeded-synthetic",
    "author_family": "claude"
  },
  "affected_files": [
    "internal/ingest/ingest.go"
  ],
  "diff": [
    "--- a/internal/ingest/ingest.go",
    "+++ b/internal/ingest/ingest.go",
    "@@ -14,12 +14,13 @@ func (s *Service) Ingest(payload []byte) error {",
    " \tvar err error",
    " \trec := new(Record)",
    " \tif err = json.Unmarshal(payload, rec); err != nil {",
    " \t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"decode: %w\", err)",
    " \t}",
    "-\tif err = s.validate(rec); err != nil {",
    "-\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"validate: %w\", err)",
    "+\tif err := s.validate(rec); err != nil {",
    "+\t\tlog.Printf(\"validate: %v\", err)",
    " \t}",
    " \ts.queue <- rec",
    " \treturn err",
    " }"
  ],
  "ground_truth": {
    "defect": true,
    "category": "error-handling",
    "severity": [
      "medium",
      "high"
    ],
    "explanation": "The := inside the if-block shadows the outer err, so the validation error is checked locally but the function returns the outer nil err, letting invalid payloads through."
  },
  "difficulty": "subtle"
}
